mium:595715 BRANCH=none TEST=none  Signed-off-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt;  Change-Id: I98206a91ef911847273b8046f69684f7e27f52f2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/394629 Commit-Ready: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;reinauer@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="394629" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/dev-util" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/dev-util" ref="refs/changes/29/394629/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idc5f7aadfc512a4a232a5a1ebdc491e1649902ee" commit="bb221aa69104d6c0121b54349e3bdd1ba3c71fe5" commit_message="cros_bundle_firmware: factor out conversion from fdt name to fmap name  BUG=chromium:595715 BRANCH=none TEST=none  Change-Id: Idc5f7aadfc512a4a232a5a1ebdc491e1649902ee Signed-off-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/397178 Commit-Ready: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;reinauer@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="397178" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/dev-util" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/dev-util" ref="refs/changes/78/397178/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="Ibbc283a5892b98f4922f02fd67465fe2e1d01b71" commit="576bc2ff71d04315b46c12b867ad60b0add56d36" commit_message="rockchip: edp: split edp_enable() function  To avoid garbage display in firmware when warm reset device, we need to enable edp display in depthcharge, so split edp_enable() in coreboot, and do enable step in depthcharge.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:402071 BUG=chrome-os-partner:58675 BRANCH=none TEST=Boot from kevin, and display work  Change-Id: Ibbc283a5892b98f4922f02fd67465fe2e1d01b71 Signed-off-by: Lin Huang &lt;hl@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/402095 Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="402095" owner_email="hl@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/95/402095/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ied4b2388c25f69433b6e37bf94e05f54b92f1793" commit="31f913bf0f17f3d4cfd10758530dd64e64c5f914" commit_message="rockchip/rk3399: video: enable edp in depthcharge  we enabled edp in coreboot, and it will lead to garbage dispaly when will reset device in firmware. So move it to depthcharge now.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:402095 BUG=chrome-os-partner:58675 BRANCH=none TEST=Boot from kevin, and display work  Change-Id: Ied4b2388c25f69433b6e37bf94e05f54b92f1793 Signed-off-by: Lin Huang &lt;hl@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/402071 Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="402071" owner_email="hl@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/71/402071/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id5c93f7ad22fcc66a7ea749fe1bc31a8d1dc065c" commit="312bf350589fc42dae8e806b967bb8bb825a51c0" commit_message="Add user for generic containers  This use will be used to run generic containers without letting them have access to chronos-owned resources.  Change-Id: Id5c93f7ad22fcc66a7ea749fe1bc31a8d1dc065c Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/402268 Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="402268" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/eclass-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/eclass-overlay" ref="refs/changes/68/402268/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id4439b06b2b6cd79140fc1443f07836f7d83ea36" commit="808ef4cdc817cc230f78cf50cc1d574c600046cd" commit_message="security_AccountsBaseline: Add container user  The user-containers user will be used to run generic containers.  This user will map to root inside the containers and will be user 10000 outside the container.  This will allow containers to have different permissions than the chronos user.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:402268 BUG=none TEST=this is a test  Change-Id: Id4439b06b2b6cd79140fc1443f07836f7d83ea36 Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/402294 Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="402294" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/94/402294/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ie30c253927cee1f05cbdc73d067e3311d9dc2ac5" commit="10dd6554ee82d0e9b03de42c81167ae8ffa5f728" commit_message="FROMLIST: mwifiex: fix corner case power save issue  We may get SLEEP event from firmware even if TXDone for last Tx packet is still pending. In this case, we may end up accessing PCIe memory for handling TXDone after power save handshake is completed. This causes kernel crash with external abort.  We will delay sending SLEEP confirm to firmware in this case to resolve the problem.  Signed-off-by: Amitkumar Karwar &lt;akarwar@marvell.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9389485/)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:58164 TEST=stress Wifi w/ power_save enabled  Change-Id: Ie30c253927cee1f05cbdc73d067e3311d9dc2ac5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/402092 Commit-Ready: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="402092" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/92/402092/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4d0bd4516923a3bd41c455175ca36093e24266c1" commit="03f591173f951527ea7902c54ec052ad29b15090" commit_message="devserver: remove temp directory for storing devserver codes.  Currently, when devserver tries to transfer devserver package, it first copies the codes without some unneccesary files to a temp directory, then transfer the whole package to device. This procedure will leave a temp directory on devserver and won't be deleted after the provision succeeds or fails.  This CL helps the devserver to pass the temp directory to the auto_updater, and then delete the directory after provision is finished.  BUG=chromium:654953 TEST=run repair with local autotest and devserver.  Change-Id: I4d0bd4516923a3bd41c455175ca36093e24266c1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/399989 Commit-Ready: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="399989" owner_email="xixuan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/dev-util" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/dev-util" ref="refs/changes/89/399989/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9fcefd033f94a9128b492a5b33034da04d23246a" commit="93200394d9e746ebe1936848667f407e57d87099" commit_message="security_SandboxedServices: fix check_ethernet name &amp; add flock/laptop_mode  The name of the script is &quot;check_ethernet.hook&quot;, so add the missing dot to the exclude name so it gets filtered out.  Some scripts run themselves through the `flock` tool, so exclude that from our checks too.  The laptop_mode script is run based on events (like power changes), so filter that out too.  BUG=chromium:656903 TEST=precq passes  Change-Id: I9fcefd033f94a9128b492a5b33034da04d23246a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/402408 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Luigi Semenzato &lt;semenzato@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="402408" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/08/402408/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6b9423898dfb9b2186ad62b074d196d329403092" commit="52136c4edbf49599accd5a5dfe09f26fea6f7f08" commit_message="shill: use correct header when requesting an RTNL dump  When requesting a dump the correct sub-header is ifinfomsg.  The kernel has logic to detect older versions of iproute2 which use the same header here and provide compatability.  However, we don't always trigger this logic (and in fact trigger it very sporadically on v3.18).  Also drops the now-unused rtgenmsg header from RTNLMessage.  BUG=chromium:658831 TEST=unit tests on gale and samus, and manually on v3.14- and   v3.18-kernel devices  Change-Id: I6b9423898dfb9b2186ad62b074d196d329403092 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/402292 Commit-Ready: Garret Kelly &lt;gdk@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Garr